{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789849539,"nonce":"XxpFoO1rTn2fXEBuFLl9TbjAufg=","title":"Null\u003creference\u003e into a Dynamic slot was not boxed; Map.get of a String map handed back raw bits","message":"`maybe_box_value_inner` had no `Optional` arm: a `Null\u003cString\u003e` argument to a `Dynamic` parameter passed the bare string pointer, which the receiver read as a box (`\u003cunknown type 97042433\u003e`). `Null\u003cT\u003e` over a scalar is already a box; over a reference it is now boxed as `T` (the box functions keep a null a null). Separately, `StringMap\u003cString\u003e.get` returns raw u64 bits and the extern-call result cast only knew F32/F64 for an opaque `Null\u003cV\u003e` declared type; with `V = String` the bits now cast to the string pointer, so `buf.add(m.get(k))` and `trace(m.get(k))` print the string rather than its address.","files":null}]}